\section{Telangana discrepancy}{

This table keeps Telangana as printed in Table 9, which disagrees with Table 10
of the same report by about 120,000 in every year. For 2011, Table 9 (PDF page
75) prints 13,731 thousand. Table 10 (PDF page 88) prints 38.88\% of the 35,004
thousand in Table 8 (PDF page 62), which is about 13,610 thousand.

Table 10 fits the Census. Andhra Pradesh (14,610 thousand) plus 13,610 thousand
gives the 2011 urban population of undivided Andhra Pradesh, 28,219,075. In 2011,
\code{"India"} is therefore 120,000 less than the sum of the states.
\link{population_projections_state_rural} runs low by the same amount.
